[{:db/id 17592186192781 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-8f1ed82d-67ec-55b7-826d-30733bc2c88f"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-8f1ed82d-67ec-55b7-826d-30733bc2c88f" :question/id #uuid "8f1ed82d-67ec-55b7-826d-30733bc2c88f" :question/math-academy-id "q-35575" :question/problem "Which of the following sets is a subspace of ${R}^{2}?$\n\nI. $A=\\{⟨x,y⟩\\in {R}^{2}:y=0\\}$\n\nII. $B=\\{⟨x,y⟩\\in {R}^{2}:y=3x\\}$\n\nIII. $C=\\{⟨x,y⟩\\in {R}^{2}:y=2\\}$" :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each of the subsets.\n\n- The set $A$ is a subspace. It represents a line, and a line is a subspace if and only if it passes through the origin. Here, the components of the zero vector $0=⟨0,0⟩$ satisfy the equation $y=0$ since $0=0.$ So, $0$ lies in $A.$\n\n- The set $B$ is a subspace. It represents a line, and a line is a subspace if and only if it passes through the origin. Here, the components of the zero vector $0=⟨0,0⟩$ satisfy the equation $y=3x$ since $0=3\\cdot 0.$ So, $0$ lies in $B.$\n\n- The set $C$ is not a subspace because it does not contain the zero vector. Indeed, $0=⟨0,0⟩$ does not satisfy the condition $y=2$ since $0\\ne 2.$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b99629cf-233b-5877-9205-658da974228d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b99629cf-233b-5877-9205-658da974228d" :answer-field/id #uuid "b99629cf-233b-5877-9205-658da974228d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-1382095a-ce36-5649-9176-e51b8a45eecf" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1382095a-ce36-5649-9176-e51b8a45eecf" "answer-1b5c0bb0-6a86-5a6c-bcaf-1f0fea305db4" "answer-e3d0d900-1221-5e04-8384-9a017c7b2878" "answer-d03236d8-6be8-5408-b90d-1fcabe487cf1" "answer-e18c382f-1d1e-5fc7-a402-581360ddc5de"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1382095a-ce36-5649-9176-e51b8a45eecf" :answer/id #uuid "1382095a-ce36-5649-9176-e51b8a45eecf" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1b5c0bb0-6a86-5a6c-bcaf-1f0fea305db4" :answer/id #uuid "1b5c0bb0-6a86-5a6c-bcaf-1f0fea305db4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e3d0d900-1221-5e04-8384-9a017c7b2878" :answer/id #uuid "e3d0d900-1221-5e04-8384-9a017c7b2878" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d03236d8-6be8-5408-b90d-1fcabe487cf1" :answer/id #uuid "d03236d8-6be8-5408-b90d-1fcabe487cf1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e18c382f-1d1e-5fc7-a402-581360ddc5de" :answer/id #uuid "e18c382f-1d1e-5fc7-a402-581360ddc5de" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186342187 :question/problem "Which of the following sets is a subspace of ${R}^{3}?$\n\nI. $A=\\{⟨x,y,z⟩\\in {R}^{3}:1-x-y=0\\}$\n\nII. $B=\\{⟨x,y,z⟩\\in {R}^{3}:{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}\\le 1\\}$\n\nIII. $C=\\{⟨x,y,z⟩\\in {R}^{3}:2x+3y-z=0\\}$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "activity-888de114-5cc0-5506-ab02-2950778f2cdd" :activity/id #uuid "888de114-5cc0-5506-ab02-2950778f2cdd" :activity/title "Subspaces of N-Dimensional Space: Geometric Interpretation" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048337 :activity/course 17592186046659 :activity/steps ["step-63f6444a-ffbe-508f-8985-460e2401c922" "step-353deabb-99c1-527a-9354-09b539a6e8de" "step-e64a068c-ae0d-53dd-b1d8-27da858b1eac" "step-c5ce9ac0-bc5b-50bf-a92d-9c79b7832a98" "step-769529b7-074a-511d-8739-3df09643b9d7"] :activity/first-step "step-63f6444a-ffbe-508f-8985-460e2401c922" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-63f6444a-ffbe-508f-8985-460e2401c922" :step/id #uuid "63f6444a-ffbe-508f-8985-460e2401c922" :step/content 17592186317349 :st